'''Ukrainian Baliscans''' ({{langx|uk|Українські балісканці|Ukrayins'ki baliskantsi}}; {{Langx|bl|Ucranianos baliscanos}}) are [[Baliscans]] who are of {{W|Ukrainian ancestry}}. According to the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]], there were 852,826 Baliscans of Ukrainian descent, representing 0.55% of the Baliscan population.  

Balisca has the second largest [[W:Ukrainian diaspora|Ukrainian community]] in the [[W:Americas|Americas]], and the second largest Ukrainian population outside of the [[Soviet Union]]; only the [[United States]] has a larger Ukrainian population. In comparison to Ukrainians in [[W:North America|North America]], the Ukrainian community in Balisca (as well as in neighboring [[W:Ukrainians of Argentina|Argentina]]) tends to be more descended from earlier waves of immigration and more rural. 

